WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.980
The Star Wars franchise is about to venture
into territory previously uncharted, but is

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.220
the high-stakes mission a hit or a miss?

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.980
General audiences won't be able to tune into
the first-ever live-action Star Wars series,

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.560
The Mandalorian, until it hits the upcoming
streaming site Disney+ on November 12.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.560
But a number of lucky critics have already
gotten the chance to catch about a half hour's

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.140
worth of footage from the show during a special
Disney event held on October 19.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.340
Taking to social media, these critics have
spilled their spoiler-free thoughts on The

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.240
Mandalorian, and things are looking brighter
than C-3PO after a buff and shine.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.140
"Die, Jedi dogs!

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.160
What did I say?"

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.200
In fact, many have praised the forthcoming
series everything they had hoped for...and

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:42.900
then some.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.900
Here's a round-up of the first reactions to
The Mandalorian.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.320
One of the biggest takeaways from the early
reactions to The Mandalorian is that it's

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.640
kick-ass, action-packed, and basically everything
a Star Wars fan could want from a live-action

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.140
series.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:01.239
From what critics have seen so far, it sounds
like the set pieces, aesthetic, characters,

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:05.779
and story of the show all come together to
make for a series that fans of the franchise

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:06.360
will love.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.799
Collider editor in chief Steven Weintraub
said in his reaction,

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.480
"This is the Star Wars thing I've been waiting
for!

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:17.319
While I love the Skywalker saga, I've wanted
to see new characters and places explored

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.469
in depth which can only be done over multiple
episodes in a series format.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:22.980
Cannot wait to see more."

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:23.980
He continued,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.960
"It's as awesome as you want it to be.

00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:30.470
Can't say anything specific but one scene
answered a question that I don't think has

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.600
ever been explained/shown in any Star Wars
movie.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.140
Love that it opens up the Star Wars universe
in a cool new way."

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.370
Star Wars social media manager Michelle Buchman
tweeted her prediction that fans will be very

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.100
pleased by the Jon Favreau-created series,
which she said reminded her of

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:50.399
"...old studio westerns of the 40's and 50's
with a dash of samurai movie vibes mixed in

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:51.819
a Star Wars-y blender."

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:55.080
Actress and host Jennifer Larda felt similarly,
writing,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.840
"...all I have to say is, this is the epic
Star Wars show we’ve been waiting years

00:01:58.840 --> 00:01:59.340
for.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.900
Please pardon my excitement."

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.060
She then clarified that she has nothing but
love for the animated Star Wars series that

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:09.060
have come before, like The Clone Wars, Rebels,
and Resistance.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.950
But if you've been holding out hope for a
live-action series, The Mandalorian is the

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.100
answer to your prayers.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:19.180
Entertainment Tonight producer and online
host Ash Crossan was moved to tears after

00:02:19.189 --> 00:02:23.829
watching footage from The Mandalorian, signaling
that the series is powerful enough to make

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:28.320
viewers incredibly emotional given its quality
and its true-to-Star Wars feel.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.940
She tweeted after the exclusive screening
event,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.780
"Just watched 27 minutes of Mandalorian footage
and legit cried.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:40.440
Can't say much but, This is real and it's
happening and it feels SO FREAKING STAR WARS."

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:45.189
Drew Taylor, former managing editor at Moviefone
and current co-host of the podcasts Light

00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:50.370
the Fuse and Fine Tooning, was totally blown
away by The Mandalorian, for a different reason.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.730
For Taylor, the best part of the footage he
saw was its twist: apparently, the character

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:58.010
played by Nick Nolte isn't who fans might
think he is.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.200
Taylor wrote in a two-tweet thread on Twitter,

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.060
"Wow.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.500
The Mandalorian is completely amazing.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.860
Saw nearly a half hour of footage from what
I was told were the first three episodes.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.160
Whoever you think Nick Nolte is...the answer
will surprise you.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:14.980
Also it looks as expensive as it is, they
didn't skimp with this one.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.440
Spaceships, creatures, etc all in full effect.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.060
Cannot wait for full episodes."

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:26.580
Eric Goldman of Get Fandom praised The Mandalorian
as being both very cool and very atmospheric,

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.840
with Pedro Pascal's titular character having
what it takes to immediately captivate audiences.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.980
"What is it like to be the Mandalorian?"

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.720
"Well, just look at the image.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:39.520
That's what it's like!"

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.660
He also compared the series to a couple of
action-heavy films that he's a fan of, writing,

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.940
"[It's] sometimes evoking the vibe of Rogue
One (which I adore).

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:54.220
The title character is instantly fascinating
and there are great action and suspense moments,

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.760
including some Predator vibes."

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.380
"Come on.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.880
Kill me, I'm here!

00:03:59.000 --> 00:03:59.660
Kill me!"

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:06.520
Award-winning writer and Rotten Tomatoes-approved
critic Rosie Knight gave perhaps the coolest

00:04:06.529 --> 00:04:09.670
and most promising take on The Mandalorian
when she tweeted,

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.700
"Reliving my childhood Saturday mornings watching
Star Wars.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.459
The 30 [or] so minutes of The Mandalorian
footage we saw was incredibly cool.

00:04:17.459 --> 00:04:22.120
The samurai-infused space western you've always
wanted with an ice cold lead, a bunch of rad

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.860
creatures, and a killer score."

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:29.180
IndieWire critic Tyler Hersko tweeted that
The Mandalorian exceeded expectations, and

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:33.140
should serve as a major hit for Disney+ thanks
to its high production value.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:33.860
He wrote,

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:39.440
"I just got out of the Mandalorian press screening
and gotta say, really surpassed expectations.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.560
This seems like a truly high-budget, movie-like
project.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.910
If other flagship Disney+ series have a similar
production quality, the streaming service

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.780
will definitely have a strong run."

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.660
Added Screen Rant features editor Mansoor
Mithaiwala,

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.200
"Saw almost 30 minutes of The Mandalorian
footage this morning.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.540
It's truly incredible.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:02.199
It looks like the films, feels innately Star
Wars, introduces new concepts, and adds layers

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.620
that people have been waiting to see for a
long time."

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.140
Audiences at home can witness The Mandalorian
in all its apparent glory when it hits the

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.720
Disney+ platform on November 12th.

